WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
The Difference Between Knowledge and Wisdom.
By Muchangke.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.380
We live in an age that values knowledge more
and more, yet seems to speak less

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.600
and less about wisdom.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.080
We want our children to attend the best
schools, earn the highest degrees,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.600
and study the most sought-after fields. We
hope they understand technology,

6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.200
finance,

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.320
management, and artificial intelligence.
Ideally, we want them to be capable in

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.520
almost everything.

9
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.500
As a result, degrees become more advanced,
résumés more impressive, and minds

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.160
more crowded with information.

11
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.880
But there is one question we rarely stop to
ask seriously: Does having

12
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.920
knowledge necessarily

13
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.040
mean having wisdom? Several cases I have come
across recently have caused me to

14
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:43.600
think more

15
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.390
deeply about this question. 1. A 5,000-Yuan
Prize Revealed Something Worth Far

16
00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.440
More Than 5,000 Yuan.

17
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.910
Not long ago, an incident at Shanghai Jiao
Tong University attracted public

18
00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:57.840
attention,

19
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.960
even though at first glance it did not seem
particularly serious. Two students

20
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.510
entered a competition as a team. One student
was mainly responsible for the

21
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.040
core technical work,

22
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.560
while another student, surnamed Fan, handled
matters such as registration and

23
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.320
presentation.

24
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.790
The team eventually won a prize of 5,000 yuan.
The problem began with the

25
00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.000
distribution of that money.

26
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.560
According to information later released by the
university, Fan engaged in

27
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.840
dishonest conduct

28
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.400
during the distribution of the prize money,
including falsifying a payment

29
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.360
record and

30
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.940
concealing the actual amount of the award.
After the matter came to light, the

31
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.200
university imposed

32
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.290
disciplinary action. A young person capable of
gaining admission to Shanghai Jiao

33
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.600
Tong University

34
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.570
is certainly not lacking in knowledge. He knew
how to register for a

35
00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.560
competition,

36
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.280
how to participate, how to prepare materials,
and even how to use modern

37
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.800
technology to produce

38
00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.320
a record that might appear convincing enough
to escape scrutiny. In one sense,

39
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.280
all of these are

40
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.420
forms of" knowledge." But knowing how to do
something skillfully is not the same

41
00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.840
as knowing whether it

42
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.040
should be done at all. That is one of the most
fundamental differences between

43
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:15.680
knowledge and

44
00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:21.360
wisdom. Knowledge asks," Can I do this?"
Wisdom asks," Should I do this?"

45
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.400
Knowledge is concerned

46
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.300
with methods; wisdom is concerned with
direction. Knowledge can help a person

47
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.320
move quickly.

48
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.710
Wisdom determines where that person is
actually going. If the direction is

49
00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.280
wrong,

50
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.280
the faster you travel, the farther you may end
up from your destination.

51
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:45.210
2.200 Yuan and 28 Yuan: Money Is Not What Is
Truly Expensive. Two other stories

52
00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:45.760
have also

53
00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.110
circulated online. One story tells of a young
person who had just completed a

54
00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.160
master's degree

55
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:58.550
and secured a teaching position. He reportedly
sold a gaming account for 2,200

56
00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.920
yuan, then later

57
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:06.240
used the account-recovery mechanism to take it
back. What may have seemed like"

58
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:06.880
just a little

59
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.400
more than two thousand yuan" eventually cost
him far more because of legal and

60
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.720
credibility issues.

61
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.640
Another online story is even more sobering. It
is said that a well-educated

62
00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.680
young white-collar

63
00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.660
worker with a decent income received a food
delivery worth only a few dozen

64
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.040
yuan, then complained that

65
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.390
the delivery rider had failed to deliver the
order and obtained a refund from

66
00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.480
the platform.

67
00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.000
The specific details of these online stories
may not all have been fully

68
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.160
verified through

69
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.160
authoritative sources, so there is no need for
us to rush to judgment about the

70
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.120
individuals involved.

71
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.100
But the question raised by these stories is
very real: If someone is willing to

72
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.440
sell his integrity

73
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.360
for 2,200 yuan— or even 28 yuan— then what is
truly expensive?

74
00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:03.680
The real issue has never been 5,000 yuan,
2,200 yuan, or 28 yuan. The real issue

75
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.800
is this: When

76
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.430
personal gain is placed in front of me, is
there a line in my heart that I

77
00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.040
refuse to cross? If

78
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.560
there is no such line, today it may be 28
yuan. Tomorrow it may be 2,800. One

79
00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.960
day it may be 280,000.

80
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.000
Character rarely collapses all at once in some
dramatic, earth-shattering moment.

81
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.200
More often, it is formed— or eroded— through
one small and seemingly insignificant

82
00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:33.920
choice after

83
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.120
another. Today, I take a small advantage.
Tomorrow, I tell a small lie. The next

84
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.400
day, I tell myself,"

85
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:46.000
No one will know anyway." Later, I reassure
myself," Everybody does it." Over time,

86
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:46.960
a person does not

87
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.480
suddenly lose integrity. He sells it little by
little through countless small

88
00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.320
decisions.

89
00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.240
That is why Jesus says in Luke 16: 10:" He
that is faithful in that which is

90
00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:58.720
least

91
00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:04.190
is faithful also in much: and he that is
unjust in the least is unjust also in

92
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:04.880
much."

93
00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.250
The Bible understands human nature remarkably
well. Big things are often simply

94
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.040
small things

95
00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.730
magnified. The kind of person you are when 28
yuan is at stake may very well be

96
00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.440
the kind of

97
00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:23.060
person you remain when 28 million yuan is at
stake. 3. Knowledge Is Knowing

98
00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.080
About Things;

99
00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.440
Wisdom Is Knowing How to Live. So what exactly
is knowledge, and what is wisdom?

100
00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.480
Simply put,

101
00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.820
knowledge is our understanding of things. If
you understand physics, you

102
00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.560
possess knowledge of physics.

103
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.120
If you understand medicine, you possess
medical knowledge. If you understand

104
00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.080
law, you possess

105
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.800
legal knowledge. If you understand computers,
you possess technical knowledge.

106
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.840
To a considerable

107
00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.440
degree, an academic degree demonstrates that a
person has received systematic

108
00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.280
training in a

109
00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.440
particular field of knowledge. We should
therefore respect knowledge, and we

110
00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.800
should certainly encourage

111
00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.490
our children to study diligently. The
Christian faith has never been opposed to

112
00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.400
knowledge.

113
00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:10.400
The problem is this: Knowledge is not wisdom.
A person may hold a doctorate and

114
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.040
still not

115
00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.270
know how to treat others. A person may know
the law inside and out while

116
00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.640
constantly searching for

117
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:21.820
loopholes. A person may study the complexities
of human nature and yet fail to

118
00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.120
deal honestly with

119
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:29.080
the people closest to him. A person may even
be clever enough to design an

120
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.880
elaborate deception,

121
00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:35.010
yet lack the wisdom to realize that he is
destroying something far more

122
00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.560
valuable than money.

123
00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:42.030
Wisdom does not merely answer the question,"
What is this?" Wisdom asks: How

124
00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.040
should I live?

125
00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:48.240
How should I treat money? How should I respond
to personal gain? How should I

126
00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.200
treat people who

127
00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.880
are weaker than I am? How should I handle
relationships? What should I choose

128
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:54.400
when no

129
00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.000
one is watching? If lying could benefit me,
should I still tell the truth? If

130
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.280
taking advantage of

131
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.140
someone brings no immediate punishment, will I
still hold to my principles? A

132
00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.920
degree may not

133
00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:12.780
answer these questions. Yet these are the
questions that ultimately shape the

134
00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.240
kind of person we become.

135
00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:20.880
4. Why Does Wisdom Begin with" Fear"? Proverbs
9: 10 says:" The fear of the LORD

136
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.240
is the beginning of

137
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:27.260
wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is
understanding." This is profoundly

138
00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.360
important. The Bible does not

139
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:34.970
say," Having more knowledge is the beginning
of wisdom." It does not say," A higher

140
00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.080
degree is the

141
00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.850
beginning of wisdom." It does not even say,"
Intelligence is the beginning of

142
00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.440
wisdom." It says:

143
00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:49.170
The fear of the LORD is the beginning of
wisdom. Why? Because true wisdom

144
00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.200
begins not by resolving the

145
00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.870
relationship between a person and knowledge,
but the relationship between a

146
00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.440
person and God.

147
00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.320
Why would someone choose honesty when no one
is watching? Why refuse to take

148
00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.520
advantage of an

149
00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:09.720
opportunity when it would be easy to do so?
Why refuse to bully, exploit, or trample

150
00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:10.320
on someone

151
00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:15.680
weaker? Because that person knows: People may
not see, but God sees. That is

152
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.760
what it means to fear God.

153
00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.890
The fear of God does not mean living in terror
that God is waiting for an

154
00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.920
opportunity to punish us.

155
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:29.040
It means recognizing that above my desires
there is God; above my interests

156
00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.160
there is truth; and

157
00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:35.950
above my personal choices there remains a
standard of right and wrong. I am not

158
00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.120
the final judge of

159
00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:42.660
my own life. Therefore, I cannot say," I want
it, so I have the right to take it."

160
00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.800
I cannot say," No one

161
00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:50.830
knows, so it does not matter." I cannot say,"
Everyone else does it, so it must be

162
00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.560
right." To fear God

163
00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:58.030
is to know that even where human eyes cannot
see, there is still a line I must

164
00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.920
not cross. 5. Our

165
00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:04.920
Relationship with God Flows into Our
Relationships with Others. This is also

166
00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.480
why the Bible binds love

167
00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:12.160
for God and love for others so closely
together. When our relationship with God

168
00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.600
is rightly ordered,

169
00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.690
it gradually transforms the way we relate to
other people. A person who truly

170
00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.680
fears God

171
00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:24.960
learns to be honest because God is true. He
learns to keep his word because God

172
00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.000
is faithful.

173
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.360
He learns mercy because God has shown mercy to
us. He learns self-denial

174
00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.480
because Christ

175
00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:38.240
first gave Himself for us. He learns not to
covet what belongs to others

176
00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.440
because he understands

177
00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:45.200
that the true value of life is not measured by
how much one possesses. Conversely,

178
00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.000
when reverence

179
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:51.520
for God disappears, intelligence can easily
turn into calculation, ability into

180
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.200
a tool of self-interest,

181
00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:57.460
and knowledge into a means of satisfying
desire. That is why greater

182
00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:59.200
intelligence can sometimes

183
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.870
make a person more dangerous rather than less.
If a character cannot govern

184
00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:04.480
ability,

185
00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:09.040
then greater ability may simply produce
greater damage. Knowledge is like the

186
00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.320
engine of a car.

187
00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:14.880
Wisdom is like the steering wheel and the
brakes. There is nothing to celebrate

188
00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.840
about an engine

189
00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.360
becoming more and more powerful if the car has
neither steering nor brakes.

190
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:26.340
6. What Are We Really Trying to Give Our
Children? Parents today may need to

191
00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:27.280
reconsider a very

192
00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.300
important question: What kind of people are we
actually trying to raise our

193
00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.720
children to become?

194
00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:37.280
Of course we hope they will attend good
universities. Of course we want them to

195
00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.600
have knowledge, competence, professional
skills, and a stable income. There is

196
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.480
nothing wrong with

197
00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.600
any of that. But if a child can solve the most
complicated mathematics problem

198
00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.480
yet does not

199
00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:53.680
understand honesty; if he can enter the best
university yet does not know the

200
00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:54.640
fear of God;

201
00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:58.960
if he can earn a great deal of money yet does
not know that some money should

202
00:10:58.960 --> 00:10:59.920
never be earned;

203
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:04.480
if he knows how to defeat others but not how
to love them; then something

204
00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.000
essential is still missing

205
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.310
from our education. I increasingly believe
that every person has at least four

206
00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:11.680
accounts in life:

207
00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:16.240
a knowledge account, an ability account, a
credibility account, and a character

208
00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:16.880
account.

209
00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.600
The first two may help you open a door. The
last two determine whether people

210
00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.480
will want you to

211
00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:27.840
remain inside. A degree may help someone
obtain a first job, but credibility

212
00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.120
determines whether

213
00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.990
others will continue entrusting responsibility
to that person. Intelligence

214
00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.360
may help someone seize

215
00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.650
an opportunity, but character determines
whether that opportunity will

216
00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.120
eventually be destroyed

217
00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:45.290
by his own hands. So I want to say something
to our children and to every

218
00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.400
young person:

219
00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:51.520
My child, I do not require you to become
someone who stands above everyone else.

220
00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:56.880
But I hope you will become someone others can
trust. You may never have a dazzling

221
00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.240
academic record.

222
00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:02.800
You may never hold an enviable position. You
may even live an ordinary life

223
00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.400
from beginning to end.

224
00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:09.670
But do not lose your integrity for 5,000 yuan.
Do not cross a moral boundary

225
00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.480
for 2,200 yuan.

226
00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.100
And do not let your conscience become cheaper
and cheaper for the sake of 28

227
00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:17.600
yuan.

228
00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:22.890
There are things in this world that, once
lost, cannot be bought back at any

229
00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:23.360
price.

230
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:28.410
They include your credibility, your
conscience, your character, and the trust

231
00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.600
others place in you.

232
00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.870
Conclusion: The Diploma That Really Matters.
We live in an age of exploding

233
00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:35.600
knowledge.

234
00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:41.840
Artificial intelligence cannot give us, within
seconds, information that once

235
00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:42.880
might have taken a

236
00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.890
person years to acquire. The children of the
future will almost certainly know

237
00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.440
more than we do.

238
00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:55.000
Yet what will truly be scarce in the future
may not be knowledge at all. It

239
00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.400
may be wisdom.

240
00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:01.330
Knowledge teaches us how the world works.
Wisdom teaches us how we ought to

241
00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.800
live in that world.

242
00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:08.160
Knowledge can be gained from books. Skills can
be developed through training.

243
00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.520
Degrees can be earned

244
00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:14.040
through examinations. But the Bible tells us:"
The fear of the LORD is the

245
00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.520
beginning of wisdom."

246
00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:20.880
True education, therefore, is not merely about
putting knowledge into the mind.

247
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.400
It is also about putting reverence for God
into the heart.

248
00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:29.040
When a person truly fears God, he begins to
understand what may be done and

249
00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.080
what must not

250
00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:35.430
be done; what may be taken and what must never
be taken; when he must remain

251
00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:36.240
faithful even

252
00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:41.100
if no one is watching; and when he must refuse
to sell his conscience even if

253
00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.320
doing so costs him

254
00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:48.320
something. Five thousand yuan is not much. Two
thousand two hundred yuan is not a fortune.

255
00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:54.520
Twenty-eight yuan is almost insignificant. And
yet it is precisely in such" small things"

256
00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:55.200
that a person

257
00:13:55.200 --> 00:14:00.190
writes down, choice by choice, who he really
is. A diploma is the certificate a

258
00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.200
school gives you.

259
00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:06.570
Character is the certificate life gives you.
And true wisdom is not about how

260
00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.440
much you know,

261
00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:13.040
how much you possess, or even how intelligent
you are. True wisdom is this:

262
00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.480
when the world tells you,"

263
00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:20.080
As long as you do not get caught, it is fine,"
there is still a voice within you

264
00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:20.960
that says:

265
00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:26.000
No. I cannot do this. Because I fear God. And
because I know—

266
00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:30.860
Some advantages must never be taken, no matter
how tempting. Some lines must

267
00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:32.080
never be crossed,

268
00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:37.960
no matter the cost. And some things, once
lost, cannot be recovered by even the

269
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.560
highest degree in the world.
